      "id": "clm_01M4VYR28RD2HG0Z05CDPFPACB",
      "statement": "\"Darius the Persian\" in Neh 12:22 is Darius II (424–404 BC), and the list does not reach the time of Alexander.",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": "Neh.12.22",
      "classification": "disputed",
      "reasoning": "Keil argues for Darius II: 12:22 records one enrolment while Eliashib, Joiada, Johanan and the young Jaddua lived, and 12:11 names Jaddua only as a member of the line. Josephus makes Jaddua high priest when Alexander came (Ant. 11.8.5) and his father John contemporary with a Bagoses of \"another Artaxerxes\", which would put Jaddua's tenure under Darius III. Cowley calls 12:22–23 a later addition to the book. No direct evidence for Jaddua's dates was read.",
